# glow_rune_alphabet_witness.rish -- closed GREEN rune pronunciation table (STOA90 / G1).
#
# Binds active-designing/date/20260719/20260719-220814_glow-rune-pronunciation-closed-table.md
# to glow/tokens.rye match_rune2. Device-free.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/g/glow_rune_alphabet_witness.rish

let gate = run ["sh" "tools/g/glow_rune_alphabet_worker.sh"]

# THE TARGET IS PRINTED BEFORE THE FIRST ASSERT ON IT. An assert stops the run, so a say placed
# below one is a say the reader never receives on the one occasion it was written for -- the
# refusal. The worker's own lines name the glyph and the file; this witness's sentence names
# neither. Caught by shim_reason on the lap this guard was rostered, which is the whole argument
# for rostering it: the fault had stood in the file and no pass could hear it.
say gate.out

assert gate.ok else "glow rune alphabet G1 gate failed: ${gate.err}${gate.out}"
assert gate.out contains "OK" else "glow rune alphabet G1 gate missing OK"

# The worker publishes rune_heads=N, lexer_heads=N and unnamed_heads=N; they are echoed above so a
# downstream witness reads a field rather than grepping the sentence below for a bare number
# (REDS %283).
assert gate.out contains "unnamed_glyphs=" else "worker must publish unnamed_glyphs= so the gap is read as a field"

# THE FOURTH BINDING -- THE PAGE THAT TEACHES THE RUNE (`20260911.202958`). Three bindings held the
# lexer table against a NAME: the closed pronunciation roll, the three G1 briefs, and the TAME
# family index. None asked whether `active-designing/docs/glow/runes.md` -- whose own audience line
# reads *a careful beginner writing their first Glow, and any LLM asked to help them* -- teaches the
# rune at all, and a rune stood in that hole for twenty days. `|+` barlus was named `20260822`,
# carries STOA332-336, and is folded by seven gate sources under `src/gate/`; the reference named it
# nowhere, and neither did the primer, the inventory, or any other page of the Book. It is taught
# now, and the binding is what keeps the next one from waiting as long.
#
# `book_unnamed` holds the same two glyphs the pronunciation ceiling holds, exempt for the same
# cause rather than a second one: every entry in the reference leads with its spoken name, so a
# glyph the closed table cannot pronounce is a glyph the reference cannot head an entry with. One
# custody question, two pages, one word of Keaton's to answer both.
assert gate.out contains "book_unnamed_glyphs=" else "worker must publish book_unnamed_glyphs= so the reference's own gap is read as a field"
assert gate.out contains "book_named=" else "worker must publish book_named= beside the roll's count"

# The claim line spells no count. It said "30 heads" while the field beside it published
# rune_heads=28, which is the drift REDS %283 booked and this line then repeated: the lexer table
# grew to 30 on 20260830 and the pronunciation roll stayed at 28, and no reader could see the
# difference because one number wore both meanings. The three fields above carry it now.
# invariant: this guard is proven able to red. It asserts on a delegate's result, so its own file
# demonstrated no refusal of its own until `20260909.183200`, and `standing_equipment_redleg` reads
# exactly that population -- rostering this guard took it from 53 to 54 and refused every ship's
# cold endurance run with `ceiling_raised`. The control plants seven faults in a pen checkout, requires the
# worker to refuse each in its own words, and lifts every plant back to OK, because a refusal shown
# only in the failing direction cannot be told from a tool that refuses everything. Four plants sit
# in the lexer table; three more, added `20260909.194500`, sit in the DOCUMENTS this worker binds --
# the closed pronunciation table's own witness name and sealed count, and the family index in
# `context/TAME_GUIDANCE.md`. Those bindings carry the language's vocabulary, they are edited by
# hands rather than by the lexer, and no plant reached them until now.
say "glow rune alphabet: the control -- nine plants in a pen checkout, four in the lexer table and five in the documents it binds, each refused and each lifted..."
let ctl = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/g/glow_rune_alphabet_control.sh"]
assert ctl.ok else "glow rune alphabet: the control refused --\n${ctl.out}\n${ctl.err}"
assert ctl.out contains "pass=32 fail=0" else "glow rune alphabet: the control did not prove thirty-two behaviors --\n${ctl.out}"

say "GREEN: Glow rune alphabet G1+G2 -- lexer heads, pronounced heads and unnamed heads all published above; TAME family index and tokens.rye bound; STOA90-91, bartis STOA100, barket STOA111; the gate proven able to red on nine planted faults, four in the lexer table and five in the documents it binds -- the last two the rune reference itself, a taught head struck from it and the page gone."
